{"name":"Olive Oil","hex":"#bab86c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"olive oil","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A vegetable oil, pressed from olives, and used in cooking and as a salad dressing; it is high in unsaturated fatty acids."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/olive_oil"}],"entries":[{"title":"Olive oil","blocks":[{"text":"Olive oil is a vegetable oil obtained by pressing whole olives and extracting the oil."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Oliven_V1.jpg/330px-Oliven_V1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Olive_oil","wikidata":"Q93165"},{"title":"Olive","blocks":[{"text":"The cultivated olive is a subspecies of subtropical evergreen tree in the family Oleaceae. Modern cultivars are traced primarily to the Near East, Aegean Sea, and Strait of Gibraltar. Olea europaea is the type species for its genus, Olea, which lends its name to the Oleaceae plant family. The olive fruit is classed botanically as a drupe, similar in structure and function to the cherry or peach. The term oil was originally synonymous with olive oil."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Olivesfromjordan.jpg/330px-Olivesfromjordan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Olive","wikidata":"Q1621080"},{"title":"Oil","blocks":[{"text":"Oil is a liquid with varying degrees of viscosity depending on temperature. Oil is any nonpolar chemical substance that is composed primarily of hydrocarbons and is hydrophobic and lipophilic. Oils are usually flammable and surface active. Most oils are unsaturated lipids that are liquid at room temperature."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oil","wikidata":"Q42962"},{"title":"Olive (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Olive, also called olive green, is a dark shade of yellowish green, like that of unripe 